From: RTSP-on-GE11 contributors <noreply@invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Use destroy parameters for WOW64 demuxer teardown.

wow64_demuxer_destroy() passes its local object to demuxer_destroy(), which
interprets it as struct demuxer_destroy_params.  Using the larger create
structure places the demuxer handle at a different offset, so the 64-bit Unix
side can read the wrong handle during 32-bit media teardown.

Use the matching destroy structure and initialize it before marshalling.

This is a quarantined release-intake candidate.  Drop it if the selected GE
release or its Wine pin already contains an equivalent fix.

The license of the Wine source file applies to this patch.
---
 dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c b/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
--- a/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/unixlib.c
@@ -197,5 +197,5 @@ static NTSTATUS wow64_demuxer_destroy( void *arg )
         struct winedmo_demuxer demuxer;
         PTR32 context;
     } *params32 = arg;
-    struct demuxer_create_params params;
+    struct demuxer_destroy_params params = {0};
     NTSTATUS status;
